# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/letters.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event letter_from_a_friend
# en: A Letter From {friend}
title [eb2348] = {friend}的来信
# en: {friend} has written. {~Three pages, mostly about nothing, which is the best kind.|Half of it is crossed out and the other half underlined.|There's a drawing in the margin that is probably meant to be you.} {off_campus: The castle, they say, is too quiet without you.|They're away, and they say the quiet there is the wrong kind.}
text [28b6ff] = {friend}来信了。{~三页纸，大多在说些没什么要紧的事，这正是最好的那种。|一半划掉了，另一半画了线。|页边有一幅画，大概画的是你。}{off_campus: 信上说，没有你，城堡太安静了。|他们不在学校，信上说那边的安静不对劲。}
# en: A folded letter on a windowsill, the handwriting crowded to the very edge of the page, a pressed leaf inside.
scene [26e2f7] = 窗台上一封折好的信，字一直挤到纸边，里面夹着一片压干的叶子。
# en: Write back at length
opt.left.label [7bb28c] = 认认真真写封长信
# en: {~You write until the candle gutters and spend the postage you meant for something else. It's worth it.|Four pages back, and a pressed flower of your own. You pay the extra stamp.|You write back pages and draw them in the margin, just as badly. The postage costs more than you meant it to.}
opt.left.say.1 [cbff63] = {~你一直写到蜡烛快灭，把原本打算另作他用的钱花在了邮费上。值得。|回了四页，再夹上一朵你自己压的花。你多付了一张邮票。|你回了好几页，还在页边把他们画了进去，画得一样糟。邮费比你打算的贵。}
# en: Send a short note
opt.right.label [91c7fe] = 回一张短笺
# en: {~A few lines, warm enough. They'll know you read it.|"Missing you. More soon." It says enough.|A few lines, and a drawing of them in return. They'll laugh.}
opt.right.say.1 [755e4a] = {~寥寥几行，温度刚好。他们会知道你读过了。|“想你。回头细说。”这就够了。|寥寥几行，再回赠一幅他们的画像。他们会笑的。}
# en: {~Your note is so short it reads as cross. You meant it kindly.|Two lines. You can picture their face reading it, and it isn't pleased.|A short note, and no drawing. They'll notice the missing drawing more than the words.}
opt.right.say.2 [fc7d32] = {~你的短笺短得像在生气。你本意是好的。|两行字。你能想象他们读信时的表情，不太高兴。|一张短笺，没有画。比起字，他们更会注意到少了那幅画。}

@event letter_castle_news
# en: News From the Castle
title [8eca1f] = 城堡来的消息
# en: Someone has forwarded the Lumen Ledger to you at home. {~A professor's hat has gone missing.|The lake froze, or thawed, depending on which column you believe.|There's a letter to the editor about the refectory soup, and it is furious.} It's strange to read about the castle from your old bedroom.
text [8f0788] = 有人把《流明纪事报》转寄到了你家。{~一位教授的帽子不见了。|湖结冰了，或者化冻了，取决于你信哪个专栏。|有一封写给编辑的读者来信，痛斥膳堂的汤，措辞激烈。}在自己从前的卧室里读城堡的新闻，感觉很奇怪。
# en: A copy of the academy newssheet, forwarded in an envelope, its corners soft from travelling.
scene [d5e48b] = 一份装在信封里转寄来的学院报纸，长途颠簸让纸角都软了。
# en: Read it cover to cover
opt.left.label [4fc56d] = 从头读到尾
# en: {~You read every word, even the notices. By the end you're homesick for a place you're not at.|The whole paper, twice. Home feels very far from the castle tonight, and the castle very far from home.|You read every word, down to the furious letter about the soup, and find you miss even the soup.}
opt.left.say.1 [dd08fe] = {~你读了每一个字，连启事都没放过。读完时，你想念起一个此刻不在的地方。|整份报纸读了两遍。今晚，家离城堡很远，城堡也离家很远。|你读了每一个字，一直读到那封关于汤的愤怒来信，发现自己连那汤都想念。}
# en: Just the gossip page
opt.right.label [381870] = 只看八卦版
# en: {~The gossip is excellent. You laugh out loud and have to explain it to everyone at the table.|Someone you know is in it, for something ridiculous. Perfect.|The gossip is good, but the furious letter about the soup is better. You read it aloud at the table.}
opt.right.say.1 [97c306] = {~八卦精彩极了。你笑出了声，只好给饭桌上的每个人解释一遍。|上面有个你认识的人，为了件荒唐事。完美。|八卦不错，可那封关于汤的愤怒来信更好。你在饭桌上把它念了出来。}
# en: {~The gossip is about someone you like, and it's unkind.|There's nothing in it you didn't already know. Somehow that's worse.|The gossip is all about a quarrel you'd rather not hear of. Even the letter about the soup can't save it.}
opt.right.say.2 [466e09] = {~八卦说的是你喜欢的人，而且不太厚道。|里面没有一件你不知道的事。不知怎么，这更糟。|八卦全是一场你宁愿没听说的争吵。连那封关于汤的来信也救不回来。}

@event letter_writing_home
# en: Writing Home
title [b3ea96] = 给家里写信
# en: The placement keeps you busy, and home feels further away than the miles. {~There's ink, paper and a quiet hour.|The lamp in your lodgings is good for writing.|You owe home a letter, and you know it.}
text [941b10] = 实习让你忙得团团转，家感觉比实际的路程还要远。{~有墨水，有纸，还有一个安静的钟头。|住处的灯很适合写字。|你欠家里一封信，你自己清楚。}
# en: A borrowed desk in a strange room, a half-written letter under a lamp, a map of somewhere else pinned on the wall.
scene [a9923b] = 陌生房间里一张借来的书桌，灯下一封写了一半的信，墙上钉着一张别处的地图。
# en: Write a proper letter home
opt.left.label [a92ffc] = 好好给家里写封信
# en: {~Four pages about the work, the food and the people. The postage is dear from here. You send it anyway.|You tell them everything, and in telling it you find out how much you like it here.|You owe them a letter, so you write a long one, and the debt feels paid with interest. The postage hurts.}
opt.left.say.1 [6ed788] = {~四页纸，写工作、吃食和这里的人。从这儿寄信邮费很贵。你还是寄了。|你把一切都告诉了他们，说着说着才发现自己有多喜欢这里。|你欠家里一封信，于是写了封长的，感觉连本带利都还上了。邮费让你肉疼。}
# en: A few lines and back to work
opt.right.label [b65885] = 写几行就回去干活
# en: {~Short and cheerful. It'll do, and they'll be glad of it.|"All well, more soon." True, mostly.|A few lines to settle what you owe. They'll be glad of it, and you'll owe them a longer one.}
opt.right.say.1 [be7409] = {~简短又开心。够了，他们会高兴的。|“一切都好，回头细说。”大体属实。|寥寥几行，算是还了欠的信。他们会高兴的，而你又欠下了一封更长的。}
# en: {~You write three lines and feel guilty for a week.|The letter is so brief it reads like a receipt.|You pay what you owe with three lines. It doesn't feel paid.}
opt.right.say.2 [91454d] = {~你写了三行，内疚了一个星期。|信短得像一张收据。|你用三行字还了欠的信。感觉并没有还上。}

@event letter_reading_list
# en: A Reading List
title [7ffe18] = 书单
# en: A professor has written over the break, as some of them do, with a reading list for next term: eleven titles, three of them underlined, one with "(if you dare)" beside it. {~The handwriting slopes like a staircase.|There's a coffee ring on the corner.}
text [11229b] = 有位教授在假期里写信来，有些教授会这样，附上下学期的书单：十一本书，三本画了线，一本旁边写着“（如果你敢的话）”。{~字迹斜得像楼梯。|角落里有个咖啡渍。}
# en: A long handwritten list of book titles on academy paper, a small inkblot at the bottom where the writer paused.
scene [9412bb] = 学院信纸上一份长长的手写书单，底部有个小墨点，是写信人停笔的地方。
# en: Start on the list now
opt.left.label [df9c89] = 现在就开始读
# en: {~You read the first two by candlelight while everyone else is resting. The third is the one marked "if you dare". You don't, yet.|You make real progress and lose two afternoons of holiday to it. Next term will be easier for it.}
opt.left.say.1 [b59de3] = {~别人都在休息时，你借着烛光读完了头两本。第三本就是标着“如果你敢的话”的那本。你还不敢。|你进展不小，为此搭进了两个假期的下午。下学期会因此轻松些。}
# en: Put it under the bed until term
opt.right.label [4a4931] = 塞到床底下等开学
# en: {~The list goes under the bed with your winter boots. The holiday stays a holiday.|You don't read a word, and you don't feel a bit sorry.}
opt.right.say.1 [90ed0a] = {~书单和你的冬靴一起进了床底。假期还是假期。|你一个字也没读，也一点都不后悔。}

@event letter_parcel_from_home
# en: A Parcel From Home
title [0fa1f2] = 家里寄来的包裹
# en: A parcel from home, squashed by the post: {~a cake that has become a different shape of cake|a tin of biscuits and a jar of jam|knitted socks and a fruit loaf}, and a letter that says, in four different hands, that everyone is well and the cat is not.
text [51b9c8] = 家里寄来的包裹，被邮路压扁了：{~一块已经变成另一种形状的蛋糕|一罐饼干和一罐果酱|织好的袜子和一条水果面包}，还有一封信，四种笔迹轮流写着：大家都好，猫不太好。
# en: A brown paper parcel tied with string, opened to show a squashed cake, a pair of knitted socks and a short letter.
scene [324a7a] = 一个用绳子捆着的牛皮纸包裹，打开后露出一块压扁的蛋糕、一双织好的袜子和一封短信。
# en: Share it with everyone around you
opt.left.label [c39a82] = 分给身边的每个人
# en: {~You pass it round and it vanishes in minutes. People you barely know thank you by name the next day.|You share it out to the last crumb. Someone gives you a biscuit back, out of pity.|You cut the fruit loaf into as many slices as there are hands. The socks you keep.}
opt.left.say.1 [33c1ad] = {~你传了一圈，几分钟就没了。第二天，几个你几乎不认识的人叫着你的名字道谢。|你分到最后一点渣。有人出于同情还了你一块饼干。|你把果干面包切成和伸过来的手一样多的片。袜子你留下了。}
# en: Keep it for yourself
opt.right.label [676f93] = 留给自己
# en: {~You eat it slowly, over a week, a slice a night. It tastes like your kitchen table.|You hide it under your bed and ration it. It lasts, and so does the feeling of home.|You keep the loaf for the cold nights and wear the socks to bed. Both last till the end of the month.}
opt.right.say.1 [d1c823] = {~你慢慢吃，吃了一周，一晚一片。吃起来像你家的餐桌。|你把它藏在床底下，省着吃。它撑了很久，家的感觉也是。|你把面包留到冷夜里吃，穿着袜子睡觉。两样都撑到了月底。}

@event letter_wrong_address
# en: Not For You
title [2eac86] = 不是给你的
# en: A letter arrives that isn't yours: the right house, the wrong name, a perfumed envelope sealed with green wax. It's addressed to someone you've never heard of. The seal is very thin.
text [b48d1a] = 来了一封不是你的信：门牌对，名字错，一只喷了香水的信封，用绿色火漆封着。收信人是个你从没听说过的人。封口非常薄。
# en: A sealed envelope addressed in an unfamiliar hand to a name that isn't the reader's, lying on a windowsill beside a stamp.
scene [2f479a] = 窗台上一个陌生笔迹的封好的信封，收信人不是读信的人，旁边放着一张邮票。
# en: Forward it unopened
opt.left.label [30b9df] = 原封不动转寄
# en: You write "not known here, please try again" on the back, add a stamp of your own and send it on its way. You'll never know what it said, which is how it should be.
opt.left.say.1 [9a3fdb] = 你在背面写上“查无此人，请重新投递”，贴上自己的邮票寄走了。你永远不会知道信里写了什么，这本来就该如此。
# en: Open it, just to see
opt.right.label [d16d56] = 拆开看看
# en: It's a love letter, and a bad one, full of rhymes on "moon". You reseal it carefully and send it on, feeling worse than you expected.
opt.right.say.1 [b2636c] = 是一封情书，还是一封很糟的情书，满篇都押着“月亮”的韵。你小心地重新封好寄走，心里比想象的更不是滋味。

@event letter_bookshop_bill
# en: A Bill You Don't Remember
title [d2015b] = 一张你不记得的账单
# en: A bill from the village bookshop for a book called "On Small Explosions", which you have never seen, never borrowed and never wanted. The bookseller writes that you signed for it. The signature looks a little like yours.
text [674d82] = 山下小镇书店寄来的账单，买的是一本叫《论小型爆炸》的书，你从没见过，从没借过，也从没想要过。书商说你签收了。那个签名看上去有点像你的。
# en: A crisp bill from a bookshop, an itemised list with one title circled, held up beside a student's puzzled face.
scene [ffa128] = 一张书店的账单，列着清单，其中一本书名被圈了起来，举在一个困惑的学生脸旁。
# en: Pay it and be done
opt.left.label [9a6124] = 付了了事
# en: You pay it. A week later the book arrives, and it's actually quite good. You still don't know who signed for it.
opt.left.say.1 [4adf54] = 你付了钱。一周后书到了，其实还挺好看的。你仍然不知道是谁签收的。
# en: Write back and dispute it
opt.right.label [00c863] = 回信提出异议
# en: You write a polite, firm letter. The bookseller writes back: wrong student, same name, profuse apologies, and a bookmark by way of sorry.
opt.right.say.1 [2d6831] = 你写了一封礼貌而坚决的信。书商回信说：搞错了学生，同名，连连道歉，还附上一枚书签聊表歉意。
# en: The bookseller replies with a copy of the signature and a note that she has "dealt with your sort before". You pay, and add a stiff note of your own.
opt.right.say.2 [cabe9d] = 书商回信附了一份签名副本，还说她“以前就对付过你这种人”。你付了钱，也附上一张措辞生硬的字条。
# en: The bookseller replies with a copy of the signature and a note that she has "dealt with your sort before". Your purse is empty, so you work the bill off, shelving her stock for a long, dusty afternoon.
opt.right.say.3 [1d253f] = 书商回信附上了签名的抄件，还写着她“以前就对付过你这种人”。你的钱袋空空，只好去帮她上架整整一个尘土飞扬的下午，把账抵掉。

@event letter_old_friend
# en: From Before
title [5c8cd8] = 从前
# en: A letter from someone you grew up with, from before Lumenhold. {~They're apprenticed to a cooper now.|They're getting married in the spring.|They've moved to the city and hate it.} The letter asks what magic is like. It's a good question, and you don't know how to answer it.
text [606db9] = 一个从小一起长大的人写来的信，那是流明堡之前的事了。{~TA 现在给一个箍桶匠当学徒。|TA 春天要结婚了。|TA 搬进城里，讨厌那儿。}信里问魔法是什么样的。这是个好问题，你不知道怎么回答。
# en: A letter in a familiar childhood hand, with a small drawing of a village street in the margin.
scene [050c3d] = 一封熟悉的童年笔迹写的信，页边画着一条小镇街道。
# en: Write back pages and pages
opt.left.label [a415ae] = 写上一页又一页
# en: You try to explain magic, and the castle, and what it's like to fail an exam in front of a ghost. It takes four pages and an extra stamp. It's the best letter you've written.
opt.left.say.1 [0d9849] = 你试着解释魔法，解释城堡，解释当着一个幽灵考砸是什么感觉。写了四页，多贴了一张邮票。这是你写过最好的信。
# en: Send a postcard of the towers
opt.right.label [5c4590] = 寄一张七塔明信片
# en: A postcard of the seven towers, and "It's hard to explain. Come and see?" You both know they won't. It's a kind postcard all the same.
opt.right.say.1 [5c3765] = 一张七塔明信片，写着：“很难解释。来看看？”你们都知道对方不会来。但这仍是一张温暖的明信片。

@event letter_ledger_competition
# en: The Holiday Essay Prize
title [413b7f] = 假期征文奖
# en: The Lumen Ledger's holiday issue has found you: an essay prize, "What I Did Not Do This Holiday", five hundred words, the winner printed on the front page and paid in crowns.
text [5510d3] = 《流明纪事报》的假期特刊找到了你：一个征文奖，题目是“我这个假期没做的事”，五百字，获奖作品登头版，奖金以克朗支付。
# en: A folded copy of a student newspaper with a competition notice circled in red ink.
scene [ca3ca9] = 一份折起来的学生报纸，一则征文启事被红墨水圈了出来。
# en: Write an entry
opt.left.label [e2f007] = 写一篇投稿
# en: Your essay about the lake you didn't swim in wins. It's printed on the front page, a little cut, under your name spelled right for once.
opt.left.say.1 [162172] = 你那篇关于没去游泳的那片湖的文章获奖了。它登上了头版，删了一点，署名难得拼对了。
# en: You write a good essay that doesn't win. The winner wrote about a goat. Everyone agrees the goat was the right choice.
opt.left.say.2 [4a0cae] = 你写了篇好文章，但没获奖。获奖的写的是一只山羊。大家一致认为选山羊是对的。
# en: Let someone else win
opt.right.label [23e569] = 让别人去赢
# en: You don't write a word of it, and spend the afternoon doing one of the things you didn't do.
opt.right.say.1 [85c954] = 你一个字也没写，把下午花在了做一件你没做过的事上。

@event letter_from_a_firstyear
# en: Advice, Please
title [82c643] = 求教
# en: A first-year you once showed the way to the library has written to you over the break. They're thinking of leaving. The letter is short, crossed out in places, and ends: "Did you ever feel like this?"
text [9ac181] = 一个你曾给指过去图书馆的路的一年级生，在假期里给你写信。TA 在考虑退学。信很短，有些地方划掉了，结尾是：“你有过这种感觉吗？”
# en: A short anxious letter on cheap paper, several words crossed out, a small blot where the writer pressed too hard.
scene [ed0b56] = 一封写在廉价纸上的焦虑短信，几个词被划掉，一处墨迹是写信人用力过猛留下的。
# en: Write back honestly, at length
opt.left.label [e52764] = 认真地写一封长信
# en: You tell them about your own worst month, which isn't easy to write. Next term they find you at breakfast and say they stayed because of it.
opt.left.say.1 [f41b21] = 你跟 TA 讲了你自己最糟的那个月，这并不好写。下学期，TA 在早餐时找到你，说就是因为那封信才留下来的。
# en: Send a few kind lines
opt.right.label [095653] = 写几句暖心话
# en: "Yes. It passes. Come back." It's short, and it's true. You hope it's enough. At the start of term you see them in the queue for the barge.
opt.right.say.1 [0f9557] = “有过。会过去的。回来吧。”很短，但是真话。你希望这就够了。开学时，你在登驳船的队伍里看见了 TA。

@event letter_registrar_forms
# en: Forms in Triplicate
title [13e7ce] = 一式三份的表格
# en: The registrar's office has sent forms, in triplicate, about next term: your courses, your board, your "intentions regarding extracurricular activities". There is a box marked "Other (explain)". It is very small.
text [f55f6a] = 教务处寄来了下学期的表格，一式三份：你的课程、你的食宿、你的“课外活动意向”。有一栏写着“其他（请说明）”。格子非常小。
# en: A thick envelope of forms with the academy's seal, three identical copies of everything fanned out on a table.
scene [808b43] = 一个盖着学院火漆的厚信封装满表格，所有东西都有三份一模一样的，在桌上摊成扇形。
# en: Fill them in properly now
opt.left.label [3b10e6] = 现在就认真填好
# en: An afternoon of copying your own name three times. At the start of term, your enrolment takes four minutes while everyone else queues. Smug is a feeling too.
opt.left.say.1 [ab1a4f] = 一个下午都在把自己的名字抄三遍。开学时，别人都在排队，你四分钟就选完了课。得意也是一种感觉。
# en: Leave them until the barge
opt.right.label [2dd2ac] = 留到驳船上再说
# en: You fill them in on the barge, on your knee, in the wind. One copy goes over the side. The registrar sighs at you all the way through enrolment.
opt.right.say.1 [8ebeff] = 你在驳船上，垫着膝盖，顶着风填表。有一份被吹进了湖里。整个选课过程中，教务员都冲着你叹气。

@event letter_lyra_drills
# en: A List of Drills
title [04f721] = 训练清单
# en: Lyra has written. It's a list of drills, numbered, with a note at the bottom: "Do these. You're too slow. Everyone is." There's a postscript under that, scratched out and rewritten three times and then scratched out for good.
text [d1f640] = 莱拉来信了。是一份训练清单，编了号，底下一行：“照做。你太慢了。大家都太慢。”再下面有一句附言，划掉重写了三次，最后彻底划掉了。
# en: A letter of numbered duelling drills in crisp handwriting, a scratched-out postscript at the bottom.
scene [302edd] = 一封字迹利落、列着编号决斗训练的信，底部一句附言被划掉了。
# en: Do every drill, and send your times
opt.left.label [15f2f8] = 全部练完，寄去成绩
# en: You do them in the cold every morning and post her your times. Her reply is one word: "Adequate." It's underlined, which from Lyra is a bouquet.
opt.left.say.1 [03a70a] = 你每天早上顶着寒气练完，把成绩寄给她。她的回信只有一个词：“尚可。”还画了线，这在莱拉那里等于一束花。
# en: Ask what the postscript said
opt.right.label [435145] = 问附言写了什么
# en: Two weeks later, one line: "It said: write back." Then, smaller: "You did. Good."
opt.right.say.1 [2bbcc6] = 两周后，一行字：“写的是：回信。”下面小一点：“你回了。很好。”
# en: She ignores the question entirely and sends a second list, longer, with no postscript at all.
opt.right.say.2 [cab3bf] = 她对这个问题完全不理，又寄来第二份清单，更长，一句附言也没有。

@event letter_lyra_book
# en: Foundations of Flame
title [19e259] = 火焰基础
# en: A parcel from Lyra: her own copy of "Foundations of Flame", every margin crowded with notes in red ink. On the flyleaf: "You'll only underline the wrong bits. So I've done it for you." The handwriting goes a little uneven at the end.
text [5b0778] = 莱拉寄来的包裹：她自己的那本《火焰基础》，每一处页边都挤满了红墨水的批注。扉页上写着：“你只会画错重点。所以我替你画好了。”最后几个字有点歪。
# en: A worn copy of a spellbook unwrapped from brown paper, every margin full of small, fierce annotations in red ink.
scene [652cfa] = 一本翻旧了的咒语书从牛皮纸里拆出来，每处页边都是红墨水写的小而凶的批注。
# en: Read every note in the margins
opt.left.label [4a9afd] = 读完页边每一条批注
# en: Her notes are sharp, funny and occasionally rude about the author. On page ninety there's a small flame drawn beside a paragraph, and your initials.
opt.left.say.1 [891eea] = 她的批注犀利、好笑，偶尔还对作者出言不逊。第九十页的一段旁边画着一朵小火苗，还有你名字的缩写。
# en: Annotate it back and return it
opt.right.label [4d3ceb] = 批注回去再寄还
# en: You add your own notes in green and post it back at your own expense. Her reply says you're wrong about chapter four. She keeps the book, and your notes, and doesn't cross them out.
opt.right.say.1 [0b0409] = 你用绿墨水添上自己的批注，自掏邮费寄了回去。她回信说你对第四章的理解是错的。她留下了书，也留下了你的批注，一条都没划掉。

@event letter_tobias_goats
# en: Four Pages of Goats
title [1d32a6] = 四页山羊
# en: Tobias has written four pages, mostly about goats: one has escaped, one has eaten a hat, and one is, he writes, "going through something". Tucked in the fold is a recipe for his gran's barley soup, "for when the castle food gets you down".
text [38e597] = 托比亚斯写了四页，大部分是关于山羊的：一只跑了，一只吃了顶帽子，还有一只，他写道，“正在经历一些事”。信纸折缝里夹着他奶奶的大麦汤菜谱，“城堡的饭让你难受时喝”。
# en: A long letter in a big, careful hand with a drawing of a goat in the corner and a recipe card tucked into the fold.
scene [cdd1b2] = 一封长信，字又大又认真，角落里画着一只山羊，折缝里夹着一张菜谱卡。
# en: Make the soup
opt.left.label [ae568b] = 做那道汤
# en: You buy the barley and borrow a pot. The soup is thick and plain and exactly what you needed. You write and tell him so; he writes back that his gran says you're welcome.
opt.left.say.1 [524420] = 你买了大麦，借了口锅。汤又稠又朴素，正是你需要的。你写信告诉他；他回信说奶奶说不客气。
# en: Write back with a story of your own
opt.right.label [fdb4e3] = 回他一个你的故事
# en: You send him the story of the ghost in the bathtub, at length. His reply says he read it to the goats, and that the one going through something seemed to feel better.
opt.right.say.1 [920678] = 你把浴缸里那个幽灵的故事详详细细地寄给他。他回信说念给山羊听了，那只正在经历一些事的好像好些了。

@event letter_tobias_seeds
# en: Seeds for a Windowsill
title [404277] = 窗台上的种子
# en: A packet of seeds from Tobias, tied with garden twine. "For your windowsill. They'll keep you company. Water them Tuesdays." Then, squashed in at the bottom: "Sorry if that's soppy."
text [bee9b5] = 托比亚斯寄来一包种子，用园艺麻绳系着。“放你窗台上。它们会陪着你。周二浇水。”底下挤着一行：“要是太肉麻了，抱歉。”
# en: A small paper packet of seeds tied with garden twine, a note in big careful handwriting beside it.
scene [288954] = 一小包用园艺麻绳系着的纸袋种子，旁边一张字又大又认真的字条。
# en: Plant them straight away
opt.left.label [31f418] = 马上种下
# en: Three shoots by the end of the month, leaning toward the light. You water them on Tuesdays and think of him on the other days too.
opt.left.say.1 [1f93d2] = 到月底冒出了三棵芽，朝着光倾斜。你每周二浇水，其他日子也会想起他。
# en: Write back that it isn't soppy
opt.right.label [0e8c61] = 回信说一点也不肉麻
# en: You write that it isn't soppy, and then a whole page about why. His reply is two lines long and you can tell he went red writing it.
opt.right.say.1 [4e2c28] = 你写道一点也不肉麻，然后用整整一页解释为什么。他的回信只有两行，你看得出他写的时候脸红了。

@event letter_seraphine_card
# en: Half a Sentence
title [604144] = 半句话
# en: An envelope from Seraphine with a single tarot card inside, the Wheel, and half a sentence on the back in silver ink: "Not this week but the one after, don't take the"
text [e989bc] = 瑟拉芬寄来的信封里只有一张塔罗牌，命运之轮，背面用银墨水写着半句话：“不是这周而是下周，别走那条”
# en: A single tarot card in an envelope, with half a sentence written across the back in silver ink.
scene [ca331d] = 信封里一张塔罗牌，背面用银墨水写着半句话。
# en: Try to work out the rest
opt.left.label [4089a7] = 试着猜出后半句
# en: You spend an evening with the card and every book on tarot you can find, and spend the following week avoiding stairs, carts and soup. Nothing happens. Probably.
opt.left.say.1 [e71146] = 你对着那张牌和能找到的每本塔罗书耗了一个晚上，接下来一周躲着楼梯、马车和汤。什么也没发生。大概吧。
# en: Write and ask her to finish it
opt.right.label [b3478c] = 写信请她写完
# en: Her reply comes ten days later, and finishes the sentence: "…long way round. Or do. It's lovely either way." It is, when you take it.
opt.right.say.1 [172042] = 十天后她的回信到了，补完了那句话：“……远路。或者走也行。怎样都很好。”等你真走的时候，确实很好。

@event letter_seraphine_painting
# en: A Painting of You
title [ef73c2] = 你的画像
# en: Seraphine has sent a small watercolour: you, reading under a tree in blossom, lit from one side. It is very good. You have never sat under that tree, and it isn't spring.
text [e00bbd] = 瑟拉芬寄来一幅小小的水彩画：你在一棵开花的树下读书，光从一侧照来。画得非常好。你从没在那棵树下坐过，而且现在不是春天。
# en: A small watercolour of a student reading under a tree in blossom, unwrapped from tissue paper on a desk.
scene [62b63e] = 书桌上，从薄纸里拆出一幅小水彩，画着一个学生在开花的树下读书。
# en: Hang it by your bed
opt.left.label [fe8501] = 挂在床边
# en: It's the first thing you see each morning. It makes you look kinder than you feel, and you start, a little, to feel it.
opt.left.say.1 [f624b8] = 这是你每天早上看见的第一样东西。画里的你比你感觉中的自己更温柔，而你开始，一点点地，真的有那种感觉了。
# en: Write and ask when she saw this
opt.right.label [32b429] = 写信问她什么时候看到的
# en: She writes back, "Next spring," and nothing else, and then a second letter the same day: "I hope that's all right."
opt.right.say.1 [7d6c58] = 她回信写道：“明年春天。”别的什么也没有。同一天又来了第二封：“希望这样没关系。”

@event letter_corvin_bakery
# en: The Best Bakery in the Kingdom
title [adfc9f] = 王国最好的面包房
# en: A letter from Corvin, with a map of a town you've never heard of and a cross on one corner. "Found the best bakery in the kingdom. Can't afford it. Thought you should know where it is, saint, in case you're ever richer than me. Low bar."
text [a47484] = 科尔文来信，附了一张你从没听说过的小镇的地图，一角打了个叉。“找到了全王国最好的面包房。买不起。觉得你该知道它在哪儿，圣人，万一哪天你比我有钱呢。门槛很低。”
# en: A hand-drawn map of an unfamiliar town with a cross in ink over one corner, a postscript crammed into the margin.
scene [b16f79] = 一张手绘的陌生小镇地图，一角用墨水打了个叉，页边挤着一句附言。
# en: Send him a few crowns for a pastry
opt.left.label [e868ed] = 寄几枚克朗让他买点心
# en: You fold a few crowns into the reply. His next letter is mostly about the pastry, in loving detail, and then, at the very end and without a joke: "Thank you."
opt.left.say.1 [868bcb] = 你在回信里夹了几枚克朗。他下一封信几乎全在讲那块点心，细节满怀深情，然后在最末尾，没开玩笑：“谢谢。”
# en: Write back a map of your own
opt.right.label [06c636] = 回他一张你的地图
# en: You draw him a map of every place you've found that he hasn't, with crosses and a key. He writes back that two of them are wrong and one of them is brilliant.
opt.right.say.1 [15af53] = 你给他画了一张地图，标出你找到而他没找到的每个地方，打上叉，配了图例。他回信说其中两个是错的，有一个绝了。

@event letter_corvin_no_jokes
# en: A Letter With No Jokes
title [69148b] = 一封不开玩笑的信
# en: Corvin's letter has no jokes in it. You read it twice to be sure. It says the place is too quiet, that he keeps turning to say something to you, and that he isn't used to that. It isn't signed "your favourite thief". It's just signed.
text [04e616] = 科尔文的信里没有一句玩笑。你读了两遍确认。信上说那地方太安静了，他总忍不住转身想跟你说点什么，还不习惯这样。落款不是“你最喜欢的小偷”。只是落了款。
# en: A single short page in quick handwriting, with no doodles and no crossings-out, folded very small.
scene [12b61e] = 一页短短的信，字迹飞快，没有涂鸦，没有涂改，折得很小。
# en: Write back just as plainly
opt.left.label [82f63a] = 同样坦白地回信
# en: You write back with no jokes either, and it's harder than you thought. His reply comes by return of post, and the first line is a joke, and the second line isn't.
opt.left.say.1 [19f9f9] = 你回信时也没开玩笑，这比你想的难。他的回信很快就到了，第一行是个玩笑，第二行不是。
# en: Send a joke to make it easier
opt.right.label [e1a744] = 寄个笑话缓和一下
# en: You send him the worst joke you know. He replies with a worse one, and you're both on safer ground. You wonder, later, if you missed something.
opt.right.say.1 [ca8efc] = 你把你知道的最烂的笑话寄给他。他回了个更烂的，你们都回到了安全地带。后来你想，自己是不是错过了什么。

@event letter_mir_blueprint
# en: A Letter That Folds Itself
title [059cc4] = 会自己折起来的信
# en: Mir's letter starts folding itself back up while you're still reading it. Inside is a blueprint for a self-folding letter ("PROBABLY works!!") and a page of excited tangents about hinges.
text [08a336] = 你还没读完，米尔的信就开始自己折回去了。里面是一张自折信的设计图（“大概能用！！”），外加一页关于铰链的兴奋跑题。
# en: A letter folding itself back up on a desk like a paper bird, a blueprint with arrows and exclamation marks spread out underneath.
scene [30a2dd] = 一封信在桌上像纸鸟一样自己折起来，下面摊着一张画满箭头和感叹号的设计图。
# en: Build one yourself
opt.left.label [ce7e08] = 自己做一个
# en: Wire, wax paper and one small enchantment. Your letter folds itself into a perfect swan and then, unprompted, into a slightly worse frog. Mir's reply is all exclamation marks.
opt.left.say.1 [faa571] = 铁丝、蜡纸和一个小小的附魔。你的信把自己折成一只完美的天鹅，然后自作主张地又折成一只稍差的青蛙。米尔的回信全是感叹号。
# en: Write back with improvements
opt.right.label [d39ffe] = 回信提改进意见
# en: You suggest a stiffer hinge and a slower fold. Mir writes back that you are a genius and that they've already tried it and it exploded, but in a promising way.
opt.right.say.1 [e737ed] = 你建议铰链硬一点、折得慢一点。米尔回信说你是天才，还说 TA 已经试过了，炸了，但炸得很有前途。

@event letter_mir_ticking
# en: Something That Ticks
title [d34a62] = 会滴答响的东西
# en: A small brass thing the size of a walnut, ticking softly, with a note in Mir's hurried hand: "It's a metronome. Probably. It's set to a resting heart rate. Mine, actually, it took ages. Anyway!!"
text [d5b61e] = 一个核桃大小的黄铜小东西，轻轻滴答作响，附着米尔潦草的字条：“这是个节拍器。大概吧。调成了静息心率。其实是我的，调了好久。总之！！”
# en: A tiny brass mechanism the size of a walnut ticking softly on a pillow, a note in hurried handwriting beside it.
scene [94b0cf] = 枕头上一个核桃大小的黄铜小机关轻轻滴答作响，旁边一张字迹潦草的字条。
# en: Keep it on your pillow
opt.left.label [4d185e] = 放在枕头上
# en: It ticks you to sleep every night, slightly faster than a resting heart rate. You don't mention that. Some nights it keeps you awake.
opt.left.say.1 [aab89f] = 它每晚滴答着送你入睡，比静息心率稍微快一点。你没提这事。有些晚上它让你睡不着。
# en: Write back how much you like it
opt.right.label [e76305] = 回信说你有多喜欢
# en: You write that you like it very much. Mir's reply is three pages about escapements, and then at the very end, very small: "good. i'm glad. good."
opt.right.say.1 [5b29e2] = 你写道你非常喜欢。米尔回了三页关于擒纵机构的话，然后在最末尾，很小的字：“好。我很高兴。好。”

@event letter_kael_three_lines
# en: Three Lines
title [3b7ab0] = 三行字
# en: A letter from Kael. Three lines, in careful handwriting, with a great deal of white paper below them: the weather, a star he saw, and "I hope you are well. That is the whole letter."
text [e2a01b] = 凯尔的来信。三行字，字迹工整，下面是大片的空白：天气，他看见的一颗星，还有“希望你一切都好。信就这些。”
# en: A sheet of good paper with only three short lines on it in careful handwriting, a great deal of white space below.
scene [0c0d59] = 一张上好的信纸，只有三行工整的短句，下面大片空白。
# en: Write back three lines
opt.left.label [b6a6e8] = 回他三行
# en: You write back three lines: your weather, a star of your own, and that you're well. His reply comes promptly. It has four lines. You count them twice.
opt.left.say.1 [98ce2c] = 你回了三行：你那边的天气，你自己的一颗星，还有你很好。他的回信很快就到了。有四行。你数了两遍。
# en: Write back three pages
opt.right.label [74ab93] = 回他三页
# en: You write three pages and pay the extra postage. His reply takes a long time and says only: "Thank you. I read it four times. I do not know how to answer so much." He keeps it, though.
opt.right.say.1 [a1028b] = 你写了三页，多付了邮费。他的回信隔了很久，只写着：“谢谢。我读了四遍。我不知道怎么回答这么多。”不过他把信留着了。

@event letter_kael_star_chart
# en: The Sky on Your Birthday
title [480746] = 你出生那晚的星空
# en: Kael has sent a star chart, inked by hand, with one cluster circled in pencil. The note says: "The sky on the night you were born, from here. I checked the tables twice. It is a good sky."
text [b5c1fa] = 凯尔寄来一张手绘的星图，用铅笔圈出了一小簇星星。字条上写：“你出生那晚的天空，从这里看。我查了两遍星表。是片好天空。”
# en: A hand-inked star chart unfolded on a bed, one small cluster of stars circled in pencil, a short note pinned to the corner.
scene [6c2418] = 一张手绘墨线星图摊在床上，一小簇星星被铅笔圈起，角上别着一张短字条。
# en: Find those stars yourself tonight
opt.left.label [e14a16] = 今晚亲自去找那些星星
# en: You stand outside in the cold until you find them, low over the roofs. Your feet go numb. It is a good sky; he was right.
opt.left.say.1 [e70d0d] = 你在寒风里站着，直到在屋顶上方低低的地方找到了它们。你的脚冻麻了。是片好天空；他说得对。
# en: Thank him plainly
opt.right.label [790b3e] = 坦白地谢谢他
# en: You write that it's the kindest thing anyone has sent you. His reply says "You are welcome." Below that, smaller, as if added later: "Very."
opt.right.say.1 [3fed19] = 你写道，这是别人送过你最体贴的东西。他回信写：“不客气。”下面小一点，像是后来加上的：“非常。”

@event letter_nessa_deadline
# en: URGENT
title [44fe30] = 急件
# en: A letter from Nessa, URGENT underlined three times: the Ledger needs three hundred words on holidays for the first issue of term, "interesting ones please, the last six were about weather". Deadline circled. Twice.
text [1b7daf] = 内莎来信，“急件”两个字下面画了三道线：《纪事报》开学第一期需要三百字的假期见闻，“要有意思的，上六篇都在写天气”。截稿日期圈了出来。圈了两次。
# en: A letter with URGENT written across the top in capitals and underlined three times, a deadline circled at the bottom.
scene [cadd6e] = 一封信顶上用大写写着“急件”，画了三道线，底部的截稿日期被圈了起来。
# en: Write the piece
opt.left.label [01f165] = 写这篇稿子
# en: You spend an evening on three hundred words and post them. Nessa cuts eighty, prints the rest on page four and writes back "Good. Rewrite the ending next time."
opt.left.say.1 [4915d3] = 你花一个晚上写了三百字寄去。内莎删了八十字，把剩下的登在第四版，回信说：“不错。下次把结尾重写。”
# en: Write back off the record
opt.right.label [6db94e] = 回一封不公开的信
# en: You write back with no piece at all, just how she is. Her reply has no capitals in it. It's the longest thing she's ever written that she isn't going to print.
opt.right.say.1 [9ae8c1] = 你一篇稿子也没写，只问她过得怎么样。她的回信里没有一个大写词。这是她写过的最长的一篇不打算刊登的东西。

@event letter_nessa_off_record
# en: Off the Record
title [a5d3b6] = 不公开
# en: Nessa's letter has OFF THE RECORD at the top, and then, for once, short sentences with nothing to sell. She's tired. The holidays are long. She keeps writing headlines about you in her head and crossing them out.
text [ec4fcf] = 内莎的信顶上写着“不公开”，下面难得是一些没什么可推销的短句。她累了。假期很长。她总在脑子里给你写标题，又一个个划掉。
# en: A letter with OFF THE RECORD written at the top and then, for once, a page of short, unhurried sentences.
scene [2fa8be] = 一封信顶上写着“不公开”，下面难得是一整页简短而从容的句子。
# en: Reply off the record too
opt.left.label [f9cfa8] = 也回一封不公开的
# en: You write back slowly and honestly, which costs you more than you expected. Her answer is posted the day your letter must have reached her, which means she wrote it the moment she read yours.
opt.left.say.1 [179402] = 你慢慢地、诚实地回了信，代价比你想的大。她的回信恰好在你的信寄到那天寄出，说明她一读完你的信就动笔了。
# en: Ask to see the headlines
opt.right.label [cb2616] = 要看看那些标题
# en: She sends three. One is unprintable, one is very sweet and one is "LOCAL STUDENT STILL NOT REPLYING", which is fair. You reply at once.
opt.right.say.1 [8d60fc] = 她寄来三个。一个没法登，一个很甜，还有一个是“本地学生仍未回信”，这倒公平。你立刻回了信。
